Hexagon HTP: fuse the recurrent state step of a gated delta net layer at one token

Base: llama.cpp commit c6824a9, with patch 0001 applied (matmul-ops.c). This patch does not
touch matmul-ops.c.

Files:
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/ggml-hexagon.cpp          the graph match and the switch
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/htp-ops.h             two opcodes
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/htp-ctx.h             two prototypes
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/main.c                the dispatch
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/CMakeLists.txt        the new kernel file
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gated-delta-net-ops.c the state step (the plain kernel with other pointers)
    ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/htp/gdn-conv-ops.c        the conv step (new file)
    tests/test-backend-ops.cpp                      GDN_CONV_STATE_FUSION and GDN_STATE_FUSION

How to apply, from the llama.cpp root:

    git apply patches/hexagon-fusion/0002-hexagon-htp-fused-gdn-state-step.patch
    cmake --build build-snapdragon -j

Push to the phone: libggml-htp-v79.so (ggml/src/ggml-hexagon/), libggml-hexagon.so (bin/),
and test-backend-ops (bin/). The host library changes in this patch.

Switch: GGML_HEXAGON_OPFUSION_STATE=0 keeps the unfused path, 1 forces the fusion. When the
variable is not set, the fusion follows GGML_HEXAGON_OPFUSION (1 = all, or the bit 64 of the
mask). GGML_HEXAGON_OPFUSION=0 disables it with the other fusions.

What the patch does

At one token, a gated delta net layer reads its two recurrent states with GET_ROWS, updates
them, and writes them back with CPY. The host matches two chains once per graph and emits one
op for each:

    GET_ROWS(cache_r, s_copy) -> CONCAT(., x^T) -> SSM_CONV -> SILU, CPY(view, slot of cache_r)
        -> HTP_OP_GDN_CONV_STEP
    GET_ROWS(cache_s, s_copy) -> GATED_DELTA_NET(K = 1), CPY(state tail, slot of cache_s)
        -> HTP_OP_GDN_STATE_STEP

The DSP reads the source slot index from s_copy and writes the destination slot of the CPY.
When the two slots are the same, the update is in place. The match needs one token, one
sequence, one CPY, no other reader of the replaced tensors, and no other node that touches
the cache inside the chain span. Every other case keeps the unfused path. The state_zero
SCALE of build_rs comes before the chain, thus it stays a separate op and runs first.

Numerics

The state step runs the single-token thread of the plain GATED_DELTA_NET kernel. Only the
three base pointers differ (state in, state out, attention out). The result is the same as
the unfused DSP path bit for bit. The conv step adds the d_conv products in F32 in the order
of the CPU reference, and applies the SiLU with the two HVX routines of the SILU op.

